  "question": {
    "text": "A stationary hydrogen atom in the first excited state emits a photon. If the mass of the hydrogen atom is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math>&nbsp;and its ionization energy is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi></math>, then the recoil velocity acquired by the atom is [speed of light =&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>c</mi></math>]"
  },
